  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.32\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.32 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.31\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.31 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.30\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.30 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.29\n- Zero-setup messaging: the package manifest-merges its default `FireForNetMessagingService` (intent-filter priority `-2000`), `FireForNetMessagingReceiver`, and the `firebase_messaging_installation_id_enabled` flag — no manifest edits or service subclass required. A consumer-declared `FireForNetMessagingService` subclass with any intent-filter priority >= -1000 (default priority recommended) still overrides the package default.\n- Fixes message delivery: the merged receiver/service manifest names (`com.firefornet.messaging.*`) did not match the generated Android callable wrappers (hash-based names), so message delivery crashed with `ClassNotFoundException` at runtime. The manifest names are now pinned to the generated dex classes.\n- Message delivery is replay-buffered: events arriving before the first subscriber attach are queued (bounded, drop-oldest, with an `OverflowDropped` counter) and replayed on first subscription. Cold-start notification taps surface via `GetInitialMessageAsync` and a replayed `OnNotificationOpened` event, with no `OnCreate` initialization or ordering required (the previous readme workaround is obsolete).\n\nv1.0.1-preview.28\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.28 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.27\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.27 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.26\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.26 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.25\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.25 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.24 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.23\n- Fixed: the GMS message-handled bridge task is now observed with containment - a GMS failure can no longer surface as an unobserved task exception.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.22\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.22 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.21\n- Removed the explicit Xamarin.AndroidX.Core PackageReference; GPS binding transitives flow from the binding owner (Xamarin.GooglePlayServices.CloudMessaging).\n\nv1.0.1-preview.20\n- Initial release of the Messaging Android integration package.\n- Implements all four platform contracts (IMessagingRegistrar, IMessagingEventSource, IMessagingPermissionManager, IMessagingTopicSubscriber) over the GMS CloudMessaging transport and FireForNet's native HTTPS topic client, using IFirebaseInstallations FID + FIS token as the single registration identity.\n- KeyStore-encrypted token storage and Custom Tabs-based flows are owned by the Auth packages; this package covers FCM registration, delivery events, permission management, and topic operations.",
